<span class="hl-v">const</span> LogosScene      = lazy(() =&gt; import('./scenes/Logos/LogosScene'))
<span class="hl-v">const</span> CTAScene        = lazy(() =&gt; import('./scenes/CTA/CTAScene'))

<span class="dim">// Atmosphere — additionally gated by atmosphereReady state flag</span>
<span class="hl-v">const</span> DotGrid         = lazy(() =&gt; import('./visual/atmosphere/DotGrid'))
<span class="hl-v">const</span> ThreeCanvas     = lazy(() =&gt; import('./visual/three/ThreeCanvas'))
<span class="hl-v">const</span> DepthLayer      = lazy(() =&gt; import('./visual/atmosphere/DepthLayer'))
<span class="hl-v">const</span> CursorField     = lazy(() =&gt; import('./visual/atmosphere/CursorField'))
        </pre>
      </div>

      <h3 class="cs-h3" style="margin-top:40px">Three.js budget</h3>

      <p class="cs-p">
        With Three.js in the bundle (not CDN), every byte was audited.
        The mandala sphere is a visual element rendered at 30% opacity behind
        text — the perceptual contribution of additional geometric precision
        is zero. Budget decisions accordingly:
      </p>

      <div class="cs-diagram">
        <div class="cs-diagram-label">Three.js geometry reduction</div>
        <pre>
                      Before          After           Rationale
────────────────────  ──────────────  ──────────────  ──────────────────────────────
Sphere segments       64 × 64         32 × 32         Appropriate for display size + opacity
Texture resolution    1024 × 1024 px  512 × 512 px    Imperceptible at 30% opacity
Pixel ratio cap       device (max 4)  1.5             Retina gain at 30% opacity = 0
Power preference      —               low-power       Battery + thermal, mobile especially
Reduced-motion        renders         skips entirely  WebGL context never created
        </pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── §9 · Observability Layer ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="cs-section">
